#. type: Title =
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Campaigns of Conquest"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:9
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/siege-and-fortresses.adoc:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:20
msgid ""
"These campaign rules are based on the rules written by Rick Priestly and "
"Jervis Johnson for the Mighty Empires campaign supplement designed for the "
"8th edition of Warhammer. The supplement included a map consisting of "
"hexagonal tiles and a variety of markers. Here the rules are adjusted for "
"the Warmaster environment.  Though the rules were designed primarily for the "
"original map supplement, it can be used for any map system as long as it is "
"segmented into a sufficient number of fields."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:29
msgid ""
"In our experience complex campaign systems tend to stumble and die out "
"rather quickly. The philosophy of this system is to keep it as simple as "
"possible yet still motivating to fight and contest over new territory.  In "
"the current digital age it is possible, and even more convenient to control "
"the whole campaign on-line rather than have to arrange for all the players "
"to meet together for the campaign to progress."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:32
#, no-wrap
msgid "Warmaster campaign"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:41
msgid ""
"You will need at least two (preferably three or more)  rival players who "
"will compete for territory until one player conquers the others or "
"establishes an empire of such size and power that he is declared the victor. "
"During each round of the campaign the participating players play a game of "
"Warmaster and, depending upon their degree of success, they can expand their "
"territories into their neighbours’."
msgstr ""

#.  Spelling territory
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:50
msgid ""
"The map is used to show the territory controlled by each player.  Players "
"begin with one tile marked with a banner in their chosen colour. When games "
"of Warmaster are fought, players are awarded ‘Empire Points’ that are used "
"to claim adjoining tiles as explained below. As a player’s empire expands "
"they place banners on the tiles to mark their territory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:55
msgid ""
"The winner is the first player to carve out an empire of ten tiles – this is "
"a simple way of working out who has won and you can set this target higher "
"or lower as you wish."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:56
#, no-wrap
msgid "Starting a campaign"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:68
msgid ""
"Unless you have the original supplement with plastic tiles and markers, you "
"will need to create a map divided into sufficient number of hexagonal tiles. "
"The map needs to have at least seven tiles for each player taking part. "
"There are various tile types. The rules distinguish common wood/countryside "
"tiles, river tiles, mountain tiles and shore tiles. You will also need "
"banner markers in a distinctive colour for each player. Further markers used "
"in the rules are mines, ports, castles, cities and objectives."
msgstr ""

#.  Spelling available (twice)
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:81
msgid ""
"Once you have a map, each player chooses a capital city from amongst the "
"cities on the campaign map. Choose an order in which players pick an "
"unclaimed city from the map. A capital cannot be chosen next to another "
"capital – there must be a gap of at least 1 tile between them. If there are "
"no available capital cities left on the map then the player may add a new "
"city to claim as their capital. Once each player has selected their capital "
"you are ready to play. Note that no others tiles are claimed at this stage – "
"players will get to do that as the game progresses."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:86
msgid ""
"It is good idea to place some objectives on the map to motivate players to "
"fight over them (see <<objectives>>). These should be spread over a neutral "
"area so all players have a similar chance to reach them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:87
#, no-wrap
msgid "The largest empire"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:95
msgid ""
"During the campaign players will often need to do things in a certain order "
"depending on the size of their empires.  This is determined by counting the "
"number of tiles each player controls [.edit]#at the start of each turn#.  "
"City tiles count as two tiles when working out the size of a player’s empire."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:99
msgid ""
"Break any ties with the number of cities, then the number of castles, and "
"finally a dice roll."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:102
msgid "This order remains for the whole turn, even if circumstances change."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:103
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sequence of play"
msgstr ""

#.  Extra paragraph removed
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:122
msgid ""
"The campaign is fought over a number of rounds.  Ideally, all players will "
"be present for each round or alternatively (and more likely) games can be "
"organised online through internet forums. There are also many online dice "
"roll rooms on the internet these days, which are ideal to solve all the "
"required rolls online. A typical group of players will usually work through "
"one round every week, but it all depends on how often you can get together. "
"It is even possible to play a whole campaign over a single weekend. At the "
"end of each round, players must organise and play any Warmaster games that "
"are required the before next round can proceed. In each round all players "
"work their way through the following sequence of play. All the players carry "
"out the event phase, then all carry out the revenue phase, and so on."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:124
msgid "<<events-phase>>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:125
msgid "<<revenue-phase>>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:126
msgid "<<challenge-phase>>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:127
msgid "<<battle-phase>>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:128
msgid "<<conquest-and-building-phase>>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:130
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Events phase"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:137
msgid ""
"Each player picks one event from the event chart, starting with the player "
"with the smallest empire. A player cannot pick an event that has already "
"been chosen by another player, unless all the events have already been "
"chosen at least once."
msgstr ""

#.  Spelling receive (4)
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:141
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Fool’s Gold* – Pick a Player. That player cannot\n"
"collect any revenue during this round.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:145
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Building Boom* – You may place a castle, mine or\n"
"port on any tile that you control, or replace a castle\n"
"you control with a city.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:149
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Disaster* – Pick one player. They must roll a D6 for\n"
"each castle, city, port or mine. On a roll of 1 it\n"
"is destroyed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:154
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*All or Nothing* – You receive an extra 2 empire\n"
"points this round as long as you don’t lose or draw\n"
"any battles. If you lose or draw then you receive no\n"
"empire points at all this round.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:159
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Scouts* – In any battles you fight in this round, your\n"
"opponent must deploy their whole army before you\n"
"deploy your army, and you decide who gets the first\n"
"turn.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:162
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Diplomacy* – Pick one player. They may not issue a\n"
"challenge against you this round.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:165
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Land Grab* – The first tile you claim this turn only\n"
"costs 1 empire point rather than the normal 2.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:168
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Elite Army* – In any battles you fight this round, you\n"
"may take one unit over the Min/Max limit.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:172
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Revenue phase"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:179
msgid ""
"Each player collects revenue from any mines they control. The gold is added "
"to the player’s treasury each round and can be spent or saved up to spend in "
"future rounds. Players must keep track of how much gold they have."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:183
msgid ""
"Mines generate 2D6 × 10 gold pieces each round if they are on a river tile, "
"and 3D6 × 10 gold pieces each round if they are on a mountain tile."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:184
#, no-wrap
msgid "Exhausting a mine"
msgstr ""

#.  Spelling e.g., later
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:193
msgid ""
"If all of the dice rolls are the same (e.g. 1–1 on a river, or 5–5–5 on a "
"mountain) then the mine is exhausted. Collect revenue as normal and then "
"remove the mine from the map, but leave the banner behind to show who "
"controls the tile. A new marker may be created on the tile later in the game "
"if desired."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:197
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Challenge phase"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:205
msgid ""
"Each player must issue a challenge to another player, starting with the "
"player with the smallest empire. The challenger and the player they "
"challenged must fight a Warmaster battle in the battle phase. A player who "
"has been challenged cannot issue a challenge that round – his army is "
"already committed to battle!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:206
#, no-wrap
msgid "Forming a team"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:215
msgid ""
"A player can challenge a player who has already been challenged to a battle. "
"The player who has been challenged can choose to either fight one battle "
"against all his challengers (see <<team-battles>>), or he can choose to "
"fight a series of individual one-on-one battles against each of his "
"challengers in turn (see <<multiple-battles>>). Any number of players can "
"form a team in this way."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:216
#, no-wrap
msgid "Breaking up a team"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:222
msgid ""
"A player can challenge a player who is already part of a team – this will "
"break up the team. For example, if Andy and Phil have formed a team against "
"Bob, then Max could challenge one of them in order to break up the team."
msgstr ""

#.  Spelling leaving
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:233
msgid ""
"If you do this then the player you have challenged fights a battle with you, "
"leaving the remaining team member(s) to fight their opponent.  So, carrying "
"on our example, if Max challenges Phil, then Max and Phil fight a battle, "
"leaving Andy to fight against Bob."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:237
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Battle phase"
msgstr ""

#.  Spelling preferred
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:246
msgid ""
"Players can agree to fight battles of whatever size they find convenient – "
"there is no need for all battles to be fought at a preset size or with a pre-"
"selected army list.  Just play Warmaster games as you normally would at "
"1000pts, 2000pts, 3000pts or whatever is your preferred size."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:247
#, no-wrap
msgid "Army bonuses"
msgstr ""

#.  Spelling receives
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:252
msgid "Each player receives a bonus to use when they select their army."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:257
msgid ""
"The player who has the largest empire receives a bonus of ¹⁄₄₀ of the total "
"army points. So in 2000pts battle he may field 2050pts, in 1000pts he may "
"field 1025pts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:262
msgid ""
"Any player may spend up to 200 gold pieces from his treasury to add extra "
"points to their army. [.edit]#Each gold piece increases the player’s points "
"limit by ¹⁄₂₀₀₀ (0.05%), so spending the maximum 200 gold pieces adds ¹⁄₁₀ "
"(10%) to the total army points limit.#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:281
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|Gold spent |Percentage |pass:[<input type=\"number\" id=\"spend-gold-army\" name=\"spend-gold-army\" min=\"200\" max=\"10000\" step=\"5\" value=\"1000\" />pt army] |2000pt army |3000pt army\n"
"\n"
"|pass:[<input type=\"number\" id=\"spend-gold-gold\" name=\"spend-gold-gold\" min=\"1\" max=\"200\" value=\"1\" />]\n"
"|pass:[<span id=\"spend-gold-pc\">0.05%</span>]\n"
"|pass:[<span id=\"spend-gold-1000\">1000.5</span>]\n"
"|pass:[<span id=\"spend-gold-2000\">2001</span>]\n"
"|pass:[<span id=\"spend-gold-3000\">3001.5</span>]\n"
"\n"
"|10\t|0.5%\t|1005\t|2010\t|3015\n"
"|20\t|1.0%\t|1010\t|2020\t|3030\n"
"|50\t|2.5%\t|1025\t|2050\t|3075\n"
"|100\t|5.0%\t|1050\t|2100\t|3150\n"
"|150\t|7.5%\t|1075\t|2150\t|3225\n"
"|200\t|10.0%\t|1100\t|2200\t|3300\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block +
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:287
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<script type=\"text/javascript\">\n"
"    gold = document.querySelector('#spend-gold-gold');\n"
"    army = document.querySelector('#spend-gold-army');\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block +
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:291
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    function calculate_gold() {\n"
"        pc = (gold.value/10 * 0.005);\n"
"        display_pc = Math.round(pc*10000)/100 + \"%\";\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block +
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:293
#, no-wrap
msgid "        points = army.value;\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block +
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:295
#, no-wrap
msgid "        console.log(\"Gold \", gold.value, \"Army \", army.value);\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block +
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:301
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        document.querySelector('#spend-gold-pc').innerHTML = display_pc;\n"
"        document.querySelector('#spend-gold-1000').innerHTML = Math.floor(points * (1+pc));\n"
"        document.querySelector('#spend-gold-2000').innerHTML = Math.floor(2000 * (1+pc));\n"
"        document.querySelector('#spend-gold-3000').innerHTML = Math.floor(3000 * (1+pc));\n"
"    }\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block +
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:306
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    gold.addEventListener('change', () => calculate_gold());\n"
"    army.addEventListener('change', () => calculate_gold());\n"
"    calculate_gold();\n"
"</script>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:309
#, no-wrap
msgid "Multiple battles"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:316
msgid ""
"Sometimes a player will have to fight more than one battle in a round (see "
"<<challenge-phase>>). A player can use all bonuses they are entitled to in "
"each and every battle they fight that round. However, gold spent in one "
"battle is used up, and may not be used again in a later battle."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:317
#, no-wrap
msgid "Team battles"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:327
msgid ""
"Sometimes players will fight together as a team (see <<challenge-phase>>). "
"When this happens the team must split the total points value of their force "
"between all the players in the team in a mutually agreeable manner. For "
"example in a 2000 point game a two-player team might take 1000 points each, "
"or one might take 1500 and the other 500 and so on. Each player is then "
"allowed to add bonuses to their individual total as described above."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:332
msgid ""
"Each player in a team controls his own army.  Both players move their units "
"in the movement phase, both players shoot in the shooting phase etc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:336
msgid ""
"Units may not charge, shoot or cast magic spells against units controlled by "
"another player in the team."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:339
msgid ""
"Characters from one army may not join units belonging to another team "
"member’s army."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:342
msgid "Commanders can only command units from their army."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:345
msgid "Wizards can only cast bonus spells on their own troops."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:350
msgid ""
"Only units that belong to the same army count as “friendly units” as defined "
"by the rules. Units belonging to another team member’s army do not count as "
"friendly units."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:354
msgid ""
"In team battles the break point of the whole team’s army is combined, so a "
"side’s armies withdraw only when total break point is reached."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:359
msgid ""
"Each army has its own general. If one general is killed, their army doesn’t "
"withdraw, however the team can no longer win the battle. They can only lose "
"or draw."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:363
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Conquest and building phase"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:373
msgid ""
"When you play a game of Warmaster you earn empire points as shown on the "
"chart below. Empire points are used to take territory, to build cities, "
"castles, ports or mines or to remove territory from a rival player. Players "
"take it in turns to spend their empire points, starting with the player with "
"the smallest empire and working up."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:374
#, no-wrap
msgid "Earning Empire Points"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:380
msgid ""
"The number of empire points a player has to spend depends on how well they "
"did in the battle phase. Players who lose earn 1 point, drawing players earn "
"2 points, and winners earn 3, 4 or 5 depending upon the level of victory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:386
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Lose – 1 Empire Point.* The army is forced to\n"
"withdraw while earning less victory points\n"
"than the the opponent _or_ the army earns less victory\n"
"points when no side withdraws. A player also\n"
"loses when he surrenders.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:393
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Draw – 2 Empire Points.* In case one army\n"
"is forced to withdraw but gains more victory\n"
"points than its opponent the battle is a draw\n"
"and both armies get 2 points. A player also gets\n"
"2 points when no side withdraws but they have\n"
"more victory points than the opponent.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:398
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Minor victory – 3 Empire Points.* The army\n"
"is victorious when it forces the enemy to\n"
"withdraw and earns more victory points at the\n"
"same time.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:403
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Major Victory – 4 Empire Points.* The army\n"
"breaks the enemy while not losing more units\n"
"than half of its\n"
"break points.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:408
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Massacre – 5 Empire Points.* The army massacres\n"
"an enemy by forcing him to withdraw\n"
"while not losing more than 25% of its break\n"
"points.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:412
msgid ""
"In a team game all players in a team earn one less empire point (so if their "
"side wins a victory each player earns 2 empire points)."
msgstr ""

#.  2,5 changed to 2½ to avoid decimal symbol
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:420
msgid ""
"If a player fights more than one battle in a turn then they must average out "
"the empire points for the battles they fought, rounding any fractions down. "
"For example if a player fights two battles, loses one and scores a major "
"victory in the other, then they would score (1+4)/2 = 2½, rounded down to 2 "
"empire points."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:421
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spending Empire Points"
msgstr ""

#.  Spelling points
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:427
msgid ""
"Empire Points can be spent as follows. Only one unused empire point can be "
"carried over to the next campaign round."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:431
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Claim tile (2 EP)* – place a banner on a tile\n"
"without a banner that is adjacent to one of\n"
"your own tiles.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:438
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Conquer tile (3 EP)* – Replace another\n"
"player’s banner from a tile that is adjacent to\n"
"one of your own tiles with your\n"
"own. You must have fought and won a battle\n"
"against the player in the preceding battle\n"
"phase.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:441
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Build (1 EP)* – Add a castle, city, mine or port\n"
"to a tile you already control (see <<buildings>>).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:444
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Raid (1 EP)* – The player raids an unclaimed tile\n"
"to gain 3D6 × 10 gold pieces.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:452
msgid ""
"Alternatively they can raid a territory of another player. They gain "
"2D6 × 10 gold pieces from the treasury of the player whose territory was "
"raided. They cannot gain more gold pieces than the raided player actually "
"has, and also cannot raid gold guarded in castles and cities (see "
"<<buildings>>)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:460
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Plunder (2 EP)* – A player who wins a battle against\n"
"another player you can plunder one of the loser’s tiles.\n"
"Choose one of the opponent’s tile, it need not border your own.\n"
"If there is a mine\n"
"or port, remove it. If there is no building\n"
"on the tile, remove the opponent’s flag. Tiles with\n"
"castles or cities cannot be plundered.\n"
msgstr ""

#.  Break list.
#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:463
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mountains"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:466
msgid "It costs 1 extra empire point to Claim or Conquer a Mountain tile."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:467
#, no-wrap
msgid "Castles or Cities"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:470
msgid ""
"It costs 1 extra empire point to Conquer a tile that contains a castle or "
"city."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:471
#, no-wrap
msgid "Buildings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:478
msgid ""
"Players can spend empire points to build a castle, city, mine or port on a "
"tile they control. Alternatively, they may instead replace a building on a "
"tile they control with a different one. There can be only one building on "
"each tile."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:479
#, no-wrap
msgid "Castle"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:483
msgid ""
"A castle makes it more difficult for players to conquer the tile (see "
"above). Castles can also hold 25 gold pieces against enemy raiders."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:485
msgid "Castles cannot be built on marsh tiles."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:486
#, no-wrap
msgid "City"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:490
msgid ""
"To build a city there must already be a castle on the tile.  Players may "
"upgrade a castle in the same turn in which it was built, with the city "
"replacing the castle."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:494
msgid ""
"The tile counts as having a castle and in addition counts as two tiles when "
"working out who has the largest empire."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:497
msgid "Cities cannot be built on mountain or marsh tiles."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:498
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mine"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:501
msgid ""
"Mines generate gold pieces in the revenue phase. They can only be built on "
"river or mountain tiles."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:507
msgid ""
"Players can spend gold from their treasury to increase the point size of "
"your army in a battle (see <<revenue-phase>>). Gold mines on a river "
"generate 2D6 × 10 gold pieces, gold mines in a mountain generate 3D6 × 10 "
"gold pieces."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:510
msgid "Mines on tiles that are conquered are destroyed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:511
#, no-wrap
msgid "Port"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:513
msgid "Ports can be built on river or shore tiles."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:517
msgid ""
"A player with a port can claim and and conquer river or shore tiles which "
"are not adjacent to the player’s own tiles."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:518
#, no-wrap
msgid "Objectives"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:520
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mage Tower"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:523
msgid ""
"Once per battle, a player who owns a tile with a Mage Tower may add +1 to "
"their spell casting roll."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:524
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dwarf Brewery"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:527
msgid ""
"Once per battle, a player who owns a tile with a Dwarf Brewery may re-roll "
"one save roll in each round of a single combat phase."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:528
#, no-wrap
msgid "Orc Idol"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:532
msgid ""
"Once per battle, a player who owns a tile with an Orc Idol may add D3 attack "
"dice to a single unit during a single combat phase."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:535
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to win"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:542
msgid ""
"A player wins instantly when they claim their tenth tile, or if they knock "
"any other player out of the game by conquering the last tile that player "
"controls. Tiles that contain a city count as two tiles for determining when "
"a player wins the game."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:545
#, no-wrap
msgid "Siege"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:559
msgid ""
"Warmaster has a well-written siege system. Because there are fortified "
"places such as castles and cities in the campaign system it would be shame "
"not to include a the possibility of siege battles.  A siege battle requires "
"special terrain and models (fortress walls, siege towers, ladders etc.). It "
"may also slightly break the flow of the campaign. For these reasons siege "
"battles are considered only as an option for players who wish to play them. "
"There is no need to play siege battles in your campaign if you don’t want "
"to. Siege battles are played only when both players agree to do so."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:560
#, no-wrap
msgid "Into the breach!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:571
msgid ""
"When a player wins a battle and decides to conquer a loser’s tile with a "
"castle or city, he can do it either in the standard way or, if both players "
"agree, they can start a siege. When players decide to start a siege, the "
"tile is conquered for 2 empire points as usual, however the castle or city "
"remains in the defender’s hands. This tile counts as a half of a tile for "
"both players for the purpose of determining the largest empire."
msgstr ""

#.  Spelling conquer
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:582
msgid ""
"The situation remains until the castle or city is conquered or the whole map "
"tile is conquered back. To conquer the castle or city both players must play "
"the xref:siege-and-fortresses.adoc#into-the-breach[_Into the breach_ "
"scenario].  Of course, the conquering player is the attacker. If the "
"besieger wins the siege battle, they conquer the whole tile. If they fail, "
"the siege goes on.  One such attempt to conquer the castle or city can be "
"made per campaign round."
msgstr ""

#.  Spelling conquer
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:589
msgid ""
"Until the castle or city is conquered the defender has a chance to conquer "
"the map tile back in the usual manner. No extra 1 empire point is needed to "
"pay for conquering a tile with a castle or city on it as it is being held by "
"the player’s own troops."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:592
#, no-wrap
msgid "Naval operations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:604
msgid ""
"Another option to spice a campaign up is to add ship battles on sea. The "
"main task of fleets in a campaign is to support ground operations on shore. "
"Of course this is only possible when your map includes a sea. The main "
"problem is that ship battles are not included in the Warmaster rules and so "
"you would need to play them using some stand-alone rule system with its own "
"models, such as the old Man O’ War game or Armada. For this reason the naval "
"operation rules are optional and can be used only when at least two players "
"agree on that."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:611
msgid ""
"The Warmaster Rules Committee is developing rules for naval battles, based "
"on Man O’ War.  See https://www.wm-revolution.com/articles/naval-"
"battles.html[Warmaster Naval Battles] on the WRC website for rules."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:613
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set sails!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:619
msgid ""
"Naval operations can only take place at sea, not on rivers. Players who "
"agreed on involving naval operations can challenge each other to fight sea "
"battles in the same manner as in ordinary ground battles."
msgstr ""

#.  Spelling conquer
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:629
msgid ""
"A player who wins a sea battle gets a Naval Advantage over the defeated "
"player. Naval Advantage means you can conquer a shore tile of the player "
"defeated at sea for 1 empire point less (usually 2), while it costs 1 empire "
"point more for the defeated player to conquer a shore tile (usually 4) of "
"the player who has Naval Advantage over him. Note that a player still has to "
"defeat another player in a Warmaster battle in order to conquer his shore "
"tiles."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:632
msgid ""
"The Naval Advantage only makes it easier or more difficult depending on the "
"situation at sea."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:640
msgid ""
"The Naval Advantage is carried over into subsequent campaign rounds and "
"lasts until the player with the advantage is defeated in naval battle by any "
"involved player. Involved players with no shore ports can still fight sea "
"battles for Naval Advantage, however they cannot conquer another player’s "
"shore tiles until a sea port is built."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:644
#, no-wrap
msgid "Optional rules"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block *
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:648
msgid ""
"These rules are designed to give a player an additional tool to turn the "
"probability of success in their favour at critical moments of the battle."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:650
#, no-wrap
msgid "General’s abilities"
msgstr ""

#.  Spelling situations
#. type: delimited block *
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:656
msgid ""
"In the most critical of situations, a General can try to focus all his "
"efforts to avert some dire event, or the mishaps of his subordinates. There "
"are two abilities a General can use in such situations. Each of these "
"Abilities can be used once per game."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block *
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:658
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Reliable Courier:* One Hero or Wizard within 30cm of the General can re-roll a failed order.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block *
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:661
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Inspection of Arms:* One friendly unit within 30cm of the General can re-roll all dice for either one to-hit roll or armour\n"
"roll.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:664
#, no-wrap
msgid "Abstract battle resolution"
msgstr ""

#.  Change to "whatever the reason"
#. type: delimited block *
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:671
msgid ""
"To keep a campaign going players must be active.  However there are "
"situations when even the most enthusiastic players cannot find time to play "
"a battle, whatever the reason."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block *
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:678
msgid ""
"In case a player cannot fight a battle against his opponent(s) he can either "
"find a volunteer to fight it for him (no matter what army he uses) or he can "
"use the Abstract Battle Resolution system. This system is designed to decide "
"the battle with just simple dice roll.  This can happen online in a virtual "
"dice room."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block *
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:682
msgid ""
"In this roll-off the challenger is considered the attacker and the "
"challenged player is the defender. First find out a strategy bonuses your "
"army has:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:692
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|Strategy Bonus |Attacker |Defender\n"
"\n"
"|Elite army     |+1       |−1\n"
"|Scouts         |+1       |−1\n"
"|Largest empire |+1       |−1\n"
"|Each 100 gold\n"
"spent (max 200) |+1       |−1\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:695
#, no-wrap
msgid "Roll for the outcome"
msgstr ""

#.  "A" added
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:701
msgid ""
"A third person who is not involved in the battle rolls 2D6 and applies any "
"strategy bonuses. A high result favours the attacker, a low result favours "
"the defender."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/campaigns-of-conquest.adoc:711
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|Adjusted die roll |Result\n"
"\n"
"|2 or less         |Defender major victory\n"
"|3–5               |Defender minor victory\n"
"|6–8               |Draw\n"
"|9–11              |Attacker minor victory\n"
"|12 or more        |Attacker major victory\n"
msgstr ""
